  <h2 id="about">About myVideo</h2>
  <p>myVideo is Taiwan Mobile’s digital media service, offering video on demand and live channels across many devices.</p>

  <h3>Goal</h3>
  <p><span class="hl">The member center brings together a member’s plans, benefits and information, and users have to decide among many offers there.</span> A clear, intuitive structure is key to helping users find information, decide faster and feel satisfied.</p>

  <h3>Challenges</h3>
  <p>myVideo offers many kinds of membership (rentals, monthly plans, points), supports family sharing, and has several ways to sign in. The biggest challenges were pulling all of a user’s information together in a clear way, and helping existing users move past their old habits.</p>

  <h3>My role</h3>
  <p>Planned the research, built prototypes, moderated interviews, created wireframes, wrote the research report, and supported the UI design.</p>
  <p class="muted">The redesign launched on March 20, 2021.</p>

  <hr />

  <h2 id="goals">Goals</h2>
  <p>Before kicking off, we worked with stakeholders and gathered background data, and narrowed the redesign down to three goals:</p>
  <MV kind="goals" />

  <h3>Why and how</h3>
  <p>Event tracking, Google Analytics, payment funnel analysis and an early user survey all showed the same thing: the old member center had a loose, flat structure, with nothing highlighting the key information. Current plans weren’t clearly shown and couldn’t be managed online, so users couldn’t finish what they came to do and gave up.</p>
  <MS kind="old" />
  <p>On top of that, family sharing, code redemption and the member center each had their own entry point in different places, so users easily mixed up where to edit their own info versus their family members’ profiles.</p>

  <hr />

  <h2 id="research">Research</h2>
  <MV kind="method" />

  <h3>Desk research</h3>
  <p>We studied the information architecture of products whose revenue models and key features are similar to myVideo’s. This helped the team redefine the structure faster, and shaped the survey that followed.</p>
  <MV kind="competitors" />

  <h3>Survey</h3>
  <p>Before writing the survey, we first defined what we wanted to learn from it. The survey focused on <span class="hl">what users need and expect from the member center</span> and <span class="hl">how current users actually use it</span>.</p>
  <p>So we narrowed the audience to:</p>
  <MV kind="survey" />
  <p>Combining the survey results, Google Analytics, the payment funnel and competitors’ structures, we <span class="hl">regrouped the information around how users think about their membership</span>, which gave us these units:</p>
  <MV kind="ia" />

  <h3>Usability test summary</h3>
  <MV kind="usability" />

  <hr />

